 ---------MySQL-----------------------

Basic Steps to Process DB: 
1. Connecting to the database server  $con = mysqli_connect($host, $usern, $pswd);
2. Determine the required databases   $db=mysqli_select_db($Connection_var ,$Database_name)
3. Formation of SQL statement         $sql=“create database DBASENAME”;
4. Execution of SQL statement         mysqli_query($con, $sql);
5. Display the required data of record/ records 
6. Closing the connection
Connect → Select DB → Write SQL → Execute → Display → Close.

Connecting to the database server:
• Database Server
• Username
• Password
• Database name


PHP Session : session is a way to store information (in variables) to be used across multiple pages
              By default, session variables last until the user closes the browser
session variable :hold information about "one single user", and are "available to all pages" in "one application"
used to protect the site from entering the users without login
start a session in PHP:
1. Use the session_start Function
2. Automatically Start a Session

session_start
function must be called at the beginning before any output is sent to the browser.Otherwise, you’ll encounter error.

Automatically Start a Session
php.ini file :tart a session automatically (auto_start). By default, is 0  and you can set it to 1 to enable
session.auto_start = 1
